#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115242 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17602323-8777-51fe-9a70-fac173438e8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425938} {:answer/id #uuid "3745dd5b-bc8f-5c5f-bfbb-0a70d0ee8eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425940} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1862b9-030a-5755-b668-e59ca4c9e456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425944} {:answer/id #uuid "a1294db0-0da9-5a02-b9e5-791ef34dcf11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425946} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6dc1f0-4ead-53bf-8e9f-9b57805aa51d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf6dc1f0-4ead-53bf-8e9f-9b57805aa51d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425947} :answer-field/id #uuid "80130b9b-78a0-54cc-bf84-e036ce6c2ff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db005b4e-86cd-5194-b2fd-10ca4ee59c03" :question/math-academy-id "q-42021" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=3 \\\\ -3x-(k+1)y=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -(k+1) & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -(k+1) & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -k+5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}1-2y=3 \\\\ -(k-5)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=5,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+2y=3.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115242 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359439f2-81e1-5ced-8482-b2cf08a71409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425939} {:answer/id #uuid "478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425941} {:answer/id #uuid "545c0eb7-c35a-5d44-b8e2-b045ff203715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425942} {:answer/id #uuid "684ddf9d-dd44-5397-b1a8-e6e3ca6a2f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425943} {:answer/id #uuid "9720657d-4e06-51f7-8e91-da074201b940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425941} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a07998-8f4c-5e30-bdee-b2acbf389fbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84cf8820-fa64-5d50-9d9c-d3a9404788a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42059" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+3y=1 \\\\  & 6x+(k+3)y=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k-6 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=1 \\\\ (k-6)y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=6,$ then the second equation is $0=-8,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12f9fc63-1e5b-58f3-9165-48ecf337098a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324140} {:answer/id #uuid "6531f6ef-7836-5c36-8ad2-b64340ef2dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324806} {:answer/id #uuid "716e8f1f-3359-5b9c-a2b5-8043eda079e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324907} {:answer/id #uuid "942d2637-f186-5cc3-808c-b7d930c541bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325234} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ddd36b-c315-54de-90f4-9ca1832ae646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "942d2637-f186-5cc3-808c-b7d930c541bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325234} :answer-field/id #uuid "715194d1-fad4-5aa4-83e8-d5906bffa1a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e80c83a9-9107-528b-af57-73287d15e8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42061" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."}]}
